<mxCell id="semantic_model-legend" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Orange: fact tables, with their measures. Blue: dimension tables. Green: the date table. Grey: other tables. A dashed box has no key.&lt;br&gt;A line is a relationship from the many side (crow's foot) to the one side: solid is active, dashed grey is inactive, dotted red is one the plan found that a tabular model cannot express as the tables stand." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="476" width="900" height="97" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="semantic_model-notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Inactive: orders.ship_to_id -&amp;gt; addresses.address_id: it would close a cycle with orders - customers - addresses; the active path has certainty 0.8, this link 0.5. Use USERELATIONSHIP in DAX, or pick another active one.&lt;br&gt;Not related to Calendar: audit_log.happened_at (datetime with a time of day)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="589" width="900" height="80" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
